I want a plugin that shows a list of all my blorped places.
I want it to have the same look and feel as ../beings-discworld-xp-timers
It should have a "start recording" command that I run first.
Every item it finds with an identification it should log to a file.
Make sure there are no duplicated entries.
Here's an example of me looking at identified jewellery:

locate necklaces in pack
The ruby wedding necklace ("smugglers") is in the hunter's pack.
The twisting myrtle necklet ("savannah") is in the hunter's pack.
The ruby wedding necklace ("dojo") is in the hunter's pack.
The twisting myrtle necklet ("casino") is in the hunter's pack.
The twisting myrtle necklet ("lancre") is in the hunter's pack.

The identification is the string between (" and ").
It should log all identified jewellery (rings, necklaces, anklets, navel studs, earrings, bracelets, necklets, toe rings, pins). But don't limit yourself to a fixed list of jewellery types. Anything identified i look at efter /blorps_rec_start and before /blorps_rec_stop should be logged.
There should be a command to remove specific items from the list. So if "dojo" is logged from the example before I should be able to do /blorps_remove dojo and that should remove it from the list.

Ask me any questions you might need to complete the task.
Use the plugin documentation from https://mallard.vnsf.xyz/docs/mallard-plugin-dev-v0.25.0.html for any references.